cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Metalcyte in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Metalcyte: single-cell analysis on Apple silicon"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tran
    given-names: Thai Huu Loc
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1810-010X"
    affiliation: "Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Hong Hung Hospital, Tay Ninh City, Viet Nam"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/huulocmedvnu/metalcyte"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/metalcyte/"
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scRNA-seq
  - Apple silicon
  - Metal
  - GPU
  - Rust
  - out-of-core
abstract: >-
  Metalcyte is a Rust engine with a scanpy-compatible Python interface for single-cell
  RNA-seq analysis on Apple silicon. It runs preprocessing, PCA, neighbour graphs, UMAP,
  t-SNE, clustering and marker tests on the CPU cores, the matrix coprocessor and the GPU,
  and processes count matrices larger than memory out of core.
